              "transcript": null,
              "review": {
                "verdict": "changes_requested",
                "findings": [
                  "In duetflow/playlist.py:refresh_duet, when the Source Playlist or B candidate pool is empty at cold start, select returns an empty plan and `if not plan.duet` returns success before calling replace_playlist_items. A Refresh therefore makes zero PUTs, although I6 requires exactly one full replacement PUT per Refresh; the newly created Duet can remain unwritten. Rule: Every successful Refresh must issue exactly one full ordered PUT, including an empty uris replacement when the selected Duet is empty.. Scope: The empty-plan branch of refresh_duet and every Refresh path that returns success without calling write_duet.. Verify: Add a fake-transport test with an empty B pool (and one with an empty Source Playlist), run refresh, and assert exactly one PUT to /playlists/{id}/items with an empty uris array and its snapshot_id recorded..",
                  "In duetflow/playlist.py:ensure_duet and duetflow/spotify.py:create_playlist, a 429, 5xx, or transport failure raises UncertainOutcome and leaves duet.playlist_id unset, but the next refresh calls POST /me/playlists again. This can create a second real Duet when the first POST took effect before the response failed. The same automatic duplicate can follow a completed POST whose response has invalid JSON or a missing id, or a failure while set_duet_playlist writes config.yaml. Rule: Once a creation attempt may have taken effect, no later automatic Refresh may issue another create POST until the existing playlist is identified or an operator explicitly resolves the uncertainty; a returned id must be persisted safely before reuse.. Scope: Every create path from ensure_duet through create_playlist, _send_once response handling, and set_duet_playlist persistence, including failures after the remote POST and across separate Refresh invocations.. Verify: Use a fake transport that records POSTs and simulates a completed creation followed by each ambiguous response or failure (503, 429, connection reset, malformed or missing-id response), and simulate config persistence failure after a successful response. Invoke Refresh twice against the same temp config and state; assert no second POST occurs automatically, no incorrect id is persisted, and the error provides a recoverable path. Also verify successful persistence still creates once and reuses the id.."
                ],
